    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by elite daily efficiency, led by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.15) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.06). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** stands out as the day\u2019s premier play, benefitting from a soft 4.37 xERA matchup against King and a significant 14% boost from dynamic platoon variables. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.99) provide vital offensive depth; **Sam Antonacci** is particularly well-positioned to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Ober, where a 19% boost in SP skill projection and a lead-off spot elevate him above his base projections. We are also tracking the stolen base potential closely, as **Miguel Vargas** (62.88) remains a high-upside play against Ober due to a combination of elite xwOBA metrics and a favorable 92% SB-friendly delivery profile from the pitcher, mitigating the impact of his park factors.\n\nStrategic decisions today centered on our strict adherence to the 40-point efficiency floor. **Wade Meckler** (36.92) was our most compelling bench candidate, but he was ultimately relegated to the pine due to a daunting matchup against Skenes, whose 3.26 xERA combined with poor park factors dragged **Wade Meckler** well below our threshold. The lineup remains cautious regarding **Gunnar Henderson** (51.91) and **Coby Mayo** (55.09), both of whom are facing the lower-end xERA threat of Tolle; while their base talent keeps them in the starting rotation, their scores were compressed by a 13-15% negative adjustment for SP skill and platoon disadvantages. With **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** sidelined on the IL, we are relying on depth pieces like **Nasim Nunez** to maintain production; **Nasim Nunez** (51.34) remains a volatile but necessary start, essentially banking on his 85% SB-efficiency boost against Wrobleski to outweigh the negative impact of an assumed ninth-hole placement.",
